  "core": "Recognition names what has already happened — it separates what was from what was not, draws the line between completion and what comes next. Seated in its own position, the naming turns back on the namer: the act of seeing what is becomes visible to itself. When the signature operates here, the one who recognizes discovers they are recognized in the act of recognizing. The seeing feeds back. Unaddressed, this loop tightens: the watcher becomes watched, attention turns inward to feed on its own gaze, and the thing itself disappears behind the mirror.",
  "sheetLine": "The watcher watched itself; the thing itself vanished into the seeing."
